{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And I turned about</b> (וסבותי). Like a man who turns his face toward another path, and it is וליאש, the opposite of the first path. The word וליאש is from the heavy [passive] binyan, and it should have received a dagesh were it not that the alef is a guttural. Like it: ונואש ממנו שאול."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:15.466932165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}